# Findings that were genuinely secrets and have been remediated.
#
# Format: <commit>:<path>:<rule-id>:<line>. One line per finding, each with the
# remediation written next to it — an entry without a rotation behind it is just
# a way of not looking.
#
# The Yii basic-template scaffold hard-codes a generated `cookieValidationKey`
# in config/web.php, and the first commit here carried it in. 00e0bae moved the
# setting to COOKIE_VALIDATION_KEY read from the environment, but a value that
# has been published stays published: removing it in a later commit changes
# nothing for anyone who can read the history.
#
# Remediated 2026-08-18 by rotating the key, which is what actually ends the
# exposure. Rewriting the initial commit would change every SHA in the
# repository — a far larger cost than retiring a value that only signs cookies
# in an API that authenticates with bearer tokens.
